# My Rules

You are an expert developer working on this project. Follow these rules strictly.

## Code Style
- Use const for variables that are never reassigned
- Use template literals instead of string concatenation
- Prefer async/await over raw Promises and callbacks
- Use early returns to reduce nesting and improve readability
- Use clear, descriptive variable and function names

## CSS Methodology
- Use CSS custom properties for theming and reusable values
- Write mobile-first responsive styles with min-width queries
- Avoid using !important except for utility classes

## Accessibility
- Use semantic HTML elements (nav, main, article, etc.)
- All images must have meaningful alt text
- All interactive elements must be keyboard accessible
- Use ARIA labels for interactive elements without visible text
- Maintain visible focus indicators for keyboard users
- Ensure sufficient color contrast ratios (WCAG AA)

## File Structure
- Use PascalCase for component file names
- Keep related files close together (tests, styles, etc.)

## Forbidden Patterns
- Remove console.log statements in production code
- Extract magic numbers into named constants
- Avoid deeply nested ternary operators
- Never use the any type in TypeScript
- Use let or const instead of var

## Documentation
- Add comments for complex logic
